'''''Sinularia polydactyla''''', known as '''finger leather coral''', is a [[species]] of [[Octocorallia|soft coral]] in the family Alcyoniidae.<ref name="WoRMS">{{cite WoRMS|title=Sinularia polydactyla|id=209973|accessdate=14 April 2020}}</ref> Bio-active [[Chemical isolate|isolates]] called durumolides have been found in all samples of this coral.<ref>{{Cite journal|last1=Aboutabl|first1=El-Sayed A.|last2=Azzam|first2=Shadia M.|last3=Michel|first3=Camilia G.|last4=Selim|first4=Nabil M.|last5=Hegazy|first5=Mohamed F.|last6=Ali|first6=Abdel-Hamid A. M.|last7=Hussein|first7=Ahmed A.|date=2013|title=Bioactive terpenoids from the Red Sea soft coral Sinularia polydactyla|journal=Natural Product Research|volume=27|issue=23|pages=2224–2226|doi=10.1080/14786419.2013.805333|issn=1478-6427|pmid=23767460|s2cid=28077995}}</ref>

